Lintel.; Superliminare.

@AC 7847. "They shall put (the blood) upon the two posts and upon the lintel" (Exodus 12:7) = the truths and goods of the Natural... "The lintel" = the goods of the Natural. Explained. @7921. @7927.

@--. The lintel and the posts have a like signification to that of the forehead and hands. Explained, Illustrated.

Lion.; Leo.

@AC 430. "A young lion" (Isaiah 11:6) = what is opposite (to the innocence and love signified by "a calf.")

@3240[end]. Those called "Sheba and Dedan" fight for and defend the Knowledges of good and truth, and therefore they are called "young lions" (Ezekiel 38:13).

@3901[4]. It is the first state of the Church which is described by "the lion with eagle's wings" (Daniel 7:4).

@3923[3]. "Dan is a lion's whelp" (Deuteronomy 33:22). In the internal sense "a lion" = the truth of the Church, from its strength; for truth is that which fights and conquers; hence "a lion's whelp" = the first of truth, which is affirmation and acknowledgement.

@5313[15]. There were "two lions standing beside the hands;" and "twelve lions standing there upon the six steps..." (1 Kings 10:19, 20)... "Lions" = Divine truths fighting and conquering. "Twelve lions" = all these truths in one complex.

@5828[6]. The tearing to pieces of good by falsities and evils is meant in, "The likeness of the impious is as a lion; he lath longed to rend; and as a young lion which sitteth in secret places" (Psalms 17:12); "They have opened their mouth against me, a lion tearing and roaring" (Psalms 22:13); "Lest they seize as a lion my soul, rending but not rescuing" (Psalms 7:2). "A lion" = those who vastate the Church.

@6367. "Judah is a lion's whelp" (Genesis 49:9) = innocence with inborn forces. "A lion" = the good of love and the derivative truth in their power. @AE 433[4].

@--. The reason "a lion's whelp" = innocence, is that "a lion" = the good of celestial love, and a whelp is as its infant, thus innocence.

@--[2]. That "a lion" = the good of celestial love and the derivative truth in their power; and also that in the opposite sense, it = the evil of the love of self in its power, is evident from the places in the Word where "a lion" is mentioned. Illustrated.

@--. In Revelation 5:5, the Lord is called "the lion (of the tribe of Judah)" from the omnipotence which appertains to His Divine love and the derivative Divine truth.

@--. Elsewhere also in the Word Jehovah or the Lord is compared to "a lion;" as in Hosea 11:10; Isaiah 31:4; where the omnipotence of the Divine good is compared to "a lion," and the omnipotence of the derivative Divine truth is compared to "a young lion."

@--[4]. That the cherubim had the face of a lion, was from the omnipotence of the Divine truth from the Divine good, which is of Providence.

@--[5]. That the celestial, who are in power from good and the derivative truth, which are from the Lord, are meant by "lions." Illustrated.

@--[8]. That "a lion," in the opposite sense, = the evil of the love of self in its power. Illustrated.

@--[end]. In these passages, "a lion" = the power which appertains to the evil of the love of self, when it is destroying and vastating. Further illustrated.

@6369. "He bowed himself, he couched as a lion, and as an old lion" (Genesis 49:9) = the good of love and the derivative truth in their power... For when a lion bows himself, he hardens his sinews, and strengthens himself, as is the case when he sees his prey... "A lion," and "an old lion," = the good of love and the derivative truth in their power. "A young lion" = one who is in power through truth from good; and "an old lion" = one who is in power through good; for those who are in celestial good never fight, but are safe through good; for where they come the evil flee away, because they cannot endure their presence. These are they who are signified by "an old lion."

@6441[end]. The lion (like the wolf) is a rapacious animal, and it is also said of it that it seizes the prey, gathers the spoil, and preys on prey... and yet in a good sense "a lion" = truth in power from good.

@9052[3]. "The teeth of lions" (Psalms 57:4) = falsities destroying truths; "lions" = falsities from evil in their power.

@9348[4]. "A lion's whelp" = evil in its power. References.

@--. "The voice of the roaring of a lion" = falsity.

@9391[3]. Truth and the derivative good in the external form are signified by "the lion," and "the calf" (Revelation 4)... "A lion" = truth from good in its power.

@10050[2]. "A lion" (Amos 3:12) = those who vastate the Church.

@10236[5]. By "the lions" (1 Kings 7) are signified protection lest truths should enter; for "lions" = truths in their power. Explained.

@10383. Before the punishing Spirit comes, there appears to them the wide gape of a lion... @SE 1687.

@DSS 13[2]. "Their teeth were as those of lions" (Revelation 9:8) = that Sensuous things appeared to them as if they had power over all things. @AR 435. @AE 556.

@AR 241. "The first animal was like a lion" (Revelation 4:7) = the Divine truth of the Word as to power. That "a lion" = truth in its power, here the Divine truth of the Word as to power, may be evident from the power of the lion, which is greater than that of any animal of the earth; and also from the lions in the Spiritual World, in that they are images representative of the power of Divine truth; and also from the Word, where they = Divine truth in its power. @296.

@--. Hence it is that Jehovah or the Lord is compared to "a lion," and is also called "a lion." Illustrated.

@--. In these passages, the power of the Divine truth which is from the Lord is described by "a lion."

@245. By "the wings" of the lion is signified the power of fighting against evils and falsities from Hell. This power is of the Divine truth of the Word from the Lord.

@265. "Behold the lion" (Revelation 5:5) = the Lord, in that from His Own power He had subjugated the Hells, and had reduced all things into order, when He was in the world. "A lion" = the Divine truth of the Word as to power; and as the Lord is the Divine truth itself, or the Word, He is called "a lion." @AE 309.

@341[end]. Suddenly... they appeared as one great person, whose face was like the face of a lion...

@435. "A lion" = power. @451.

@471. "He cried with a great voice as a lion roareth" (Revelation 10:3) = grievous lamentation because the Church has been taken away from Him... For the lion roars when he sees his enemies and their insults, and when he sees his whelps and his prey taken away... Illustrated.

@573[2]. The reason "a lion," and "a bear," are mentioned in these passages, is that by "a lion" is signified falsity destroying the truths of the Word...

@574. "His mouth as the mouth of a lion" (Revelation 13:2) = reasonings from falsities as from truths... By "a lion" is signified Divine truth in power; but here, falsity in power appearing as truth by means of reasonings.

@--[2]. By "the lion" (Daniel 7) is signified the Divine truth of the Word in its first state, and the instauration of the Church thereby...

@875[5]. At the sides of the steps (of the Temple of Wisdom) appeared as it were lions with their whelps.

@TCR 87[2]. In that World those who are in Divine truths from the Lord are like lions, although they have no more bodily strength than sheep.

@123[end]. For Hell is like... a huge lion, to which it is also compared in the Word.

@SE 3191[2]. (A lion seen in connection with Gustavus Adolphus.)

@AE 163[3]. "A Lion" (Amos 3:12) = the Church; here, those therein who are destroying goods and truths.

@223[7]. "A lion out of the thicket" (Jeremiah 4:7) = falsity from evil. @304[9]. ( = falsity from evil destroying the truths of the Church. @637[8].)

@253[7]. "Lions" = the truths of the Church in their power; "twelve" = all. @430[12].

@278. "The first animal was like a lion" = the appearance in ultimates as to the power and the effect of the Divine truth proceeding from the Lord. "A lion" = the Divine truth proceeding from the Lord as to its power and effect.

@--[2]. That "a lion" = the Divine truth proceeding from the Lord as to power. Illustrated.

@--[10]. As by "a lion" is signified power...

@--[11]. As by lions was represented power, guard, and protection against falsities and evils, there were two lions beside the two hands of the throne built by Solomon, and twelve lions upon its six steps.

@--[12]. By "lions" is also signified the power of falsity from evil, through which the Church is destroyed and vastated. Illustrated.

@316[24]. "A lion" = falsity strongly destroying truth. @328[11].

@386[19]. "The young lions do lack and hunger" (Psalms 34:10) = those who know and are wise from themselves.

@388[9]. "A huge lion" (Hosea 13:8) = the power of falsity from evil.

@--[10]. "No lion shall be there" (Isaiah 35:9) = no falsity destroying truth.

@435[8]. That he is safe from falsities, is signified by, "he dwelleth as a lion" (Deuteronomy 33:20).

@455[17]. "Lions" (Psalms 57:4) = those who ravage the Church of its truths, and thus destroy it.

@539[7]. "Young lions" (Nahum 2:11) = the principal and protecting truths of the Church.

@556[2]. "Lions" = those who through falsities destroy the truths of the Church.

@577. "The heads of the horses as the heads of lions" (Revelation 9:17) = knowledge and the derivative thought destructive of truth... The reason "the heads of lions "here = the destruction of truth, is that "a lion" in the supreme sense = Divine truth as to power, and in the opposite sense falsity destroying truth, consequently the destruction of truth; and "the head of a lion" = the forces of the lower mind by which it destroys.

@600[14]. The reason the faces of a man and of a lion were seen to the south (Ezekiel 1:10), is that by "a man" is signified Divine truth in light and intelligence, and by "a lion" Divine truth in power thence, such as there is in Heaven in the south.

@601[4]. "A lion" is frequently mentioned in the Word, and by "a lion," in the supreme sense, is signified the Lord as to Divine truth, and in like manner Heaven and the Church as to that truth from the Lord; and thence by "a lion" is signified Divine truth as to power. @--[5].

@--[9]. Those are called "lions" who are in Divine truths.

@--[13]. "A young lion" (Ezekiel 19:3, 5, 6) = the falsity of evil in its ardour to destroy the truth of the Church.

@619[18]. Faith separated from charity, which destroys the good of charity, was represented by "the young lion" which attacked Samson with the intention of rending him. But Samson, being a Nazarite, and thereby representing the Lord as to His ultimate Natural, tore the lion, and afterwards found in its carcase a swarm of bees, and honey, by which was signified that after that faith has been dissipated, the good of charity succeeds in its place.

@650[53]. "A lion out of the forest which uttered its voice against God" (Jeremiah 12:8) = falsity of evil in the whole complex.

@654[41]. "The young lion," and the "old lion" which are over them (Isaiah 30:6) = the power of the falsity which destroys the truth and good of the Church.

@714[24]. To destroy the interior and the exterior falsities which are vastating the truths of the Church, is signified by to "tread on the lion and the asp" (Psalms 91:13); and to destroy the interior and the exterior falsities which are vastating the goods of the Church, is signified by, to "trample on the lion and the dragon."

@750[17]. "Lion" = falsities destroying the truths of the Church.

@780[6]. "A lion" = infernal falsity as to its power and desire to destroy Divine truth.

@--[7]. "The lion out of the forest which hath smitten the magnates" (Jeremiah 5:6) = the dominion of infernal falsity.

@--[10]. "I became to them as a lion" (Hosea 13:7) = the devastation of all the truth of the Church.

@781[12]. "A lion" = the power of Divine spiritual truth; and, in the opposite sense, the power of infernal falsity against Divine truth.

@--[14]. "I will devour them like a huge lion" (Hosea 13:8) = the destruction and devastation of all the truth of the Word and thence of the Church.

@--[15]. "A lion in secret places" (Lamentations 3:10) = that the interior natural man, from the evils in him, perverts all the meaning of the truth of the Word and thence of the Church, whence come falsities.

@--[16]. See <Bear-Ursus>.

@782. "A lion" = infernal falsity as to power... The reason is that by "a lion" is signified Divine truth, and therefore the Lord is called "a lion." Hence, in the opposite sense, by "a lion" is signified infernal falsity as to the power of destroying Divine truth, thus the Word, which is especially effected by means of adulterations and falsifications of it; and as the lion is an animal more powerful than all the rest, and its power increases according to its hunger to devour, thus to seize upon and tear to pieces, therefore by "a lion" is also signified the cupidity of destroying the truths of the Word. Like things are also represented by lions in the Spiritual World, for there also lions appear, but the forms of lions there are appearances originating from the cupidity of those who can powerfully adulterate and falsify the truths of the Word, by means of which the latter are destroyed; and whose power increases according to their faculty of reasoning. It is from this that by "lions" in the Word, in the opposite sense, is signified infernal falsity destroying the truths of the Church.

@1200[3]. (The lion included among animals of an intermediate character, which appear in the World of Spirits.) Lioness. Leaena.

@AC 9348[4]. "A lioness" (Ezekiel 19:2) = falsity from evil perverting the truths of the Church. @AE 280[11]. @304[12].

Lip.; Labia. Labium.

@AC 353[2]. "Lips of songs" (Psalms 63:5) = what is spiritual.

@607[2]. The Most Ancients... like the Angels, spoke by ideas, which they could express by innumerable changes... especially of the lips, in which there are innumerable series of muscular fibres which at this day are not disentangled and free... @1118[2]. @SE 530. @3322. (See @AC 1762. @7745. @10587. @10588. @10709[end]. @SE 3882.)

@1285. "The whole earth was of one lip" (Genesis 11:1) = that everywhere there was one doctrine in general. @1316.

@1286. That "a lip" = doctrine. Illustrated. @1288. @1316.

@--. "Lips" (Isaiah 6:5) = the interiors of man, thus internal worship, from which is adoration.

@1321. "Let us confound their lip" (Genesis 11:7) = that none had the truth of doctrine. "Lip" = doctrine. @1327.

@1322. "That they may not hear a man the lip of his companion" (Genesis 11:7) = that they were all discordant... "Not to hear the lip of a companion," is not to acknowledge what the other is saying; and, in the internal sense, not to acknowledge... his doctrine; for "a lip" = doctrine.

@1773. A vernal heat beginning from the region of the lips...

@1799[end]. See <Ancient Church>.

@5175. As the food is softly received by the lips... @SE 1742.

@7225. "Uncircumcised in lips" (Exodus 6:12) = to be impure as to the things of doctrine.

@7359[2]. I observed that ray lips were moved. @10587[2].

@9391[4]. "The bullocks of the lips" (Hosea 14:2)... the goods of doctrine; for "the lips" = the things which are of doctrine. @AE 279[3].

@AR 242. "The calves of the Ups" (Hosea 14:2) = confessions from the affection of truth.

@294[2]. They folded their lips... @TCR 111.

@TCR 798[6]. The Angels compressed his lips.

@SE 1342. That Spirits not instructed suppose that they have spoken to me with the lips. Explained.

@--[end]. Hence the term "lips," in the Word, = ideas, and thus thoughts.

@1631[end]. Communication by the lips = ideas apprehended by a sensuous way.

@1657. The speech of the Spirits of Jupiter with me by means of the lips and gums. Explained.

@2656. Only his upper lip seen.

@DMin 4691. That the lips correspond to truths.

@AE 130[8]. "Lips" (Malachi 2:7) = the doctrine of truth. References. @701[9].

@223[14]. "The lip of Canaan" (Isaiah 19:18) = the genuine truths of the Church.

@391[8]. "The mouth and lips" of the prophet (Isaiah 6) = the doctrine of good and truth. ( = the thought and affection, or the understanding and the will. @580[4].)

@--[13]. "The lips of Canaan" (Isaiah 19) = the genuine doctrinal things of the Church. ( = the truths of doctrine of the Church. @654[7].)

@448[15]. "I heard lips I had not known" (Psalms 81:5) = falsities of doctrine.

@453[11]. "A people of depths of lip" (Isaiah 33:19) = falsities of doctrine confirmed even to the appearance of truth. "Lip" = the truth of doctrine; here, falsity, because the people "will not be seen."

@455[2]. "Lip," "mouth," and "tongue" are frequently mentioned; and by "lip" is signified doctrine; by "mouth," thought; and by "tongue," confession... The reason is that (these three) are externals of man by means of which internal things are made public.

@--[12]. "A people deep of lip..." (Ezekiel 3:5, 6) = those who are in a doctrine which is not intelligible...

@--[16]. "The mischief of their lips" (Psalms 140:9) falsity of doctrine.

@556[9]. Under <Mouth>, see this reference.

@684[14]. "Lips" = doctrinal things.

@727[7]. "The breath of His lips" (Isaiah 11:4) = Divine truth, or the Word in the spiritual sense.

@866[4]. "Lips" = thought. @923[4].

@923[5]. "The lips," "tongue," and "breath of Jehovah" (Isaiah 30:27) = the Divine truth, which is the Word, from its ultimates to its inmosts.

Lip.; Labrum.
See <Laver>.

@AC 4791. Some (of those who love the Word, and thence long for Knowledges of good and truth) belong to the lips. -.

@--. Some correspond to the interiors of the tongue and lips, and some to the exteriors.

@4799. Their faces were prominent, especially about the lips... They said that they spoke together... chiefly by means of variations about the lips... This they endeavoured to show mo by means of an influx into my lips, by means of various foldings and windings round about them; but I could not receive the variations, because my lips had not been initiated into such things from infancy... But that speech in general can be expressed by means of the lips, is evident to me from the manifold series of muscular fibres which are folded together in the lips, and which if unrolled so as to act clearly and freely, would be able to present many variations which are unknown to those with whom these muscular fibres lie compressed. @8247.

@7807. The angelic Spirits (of Jupiter) kept... the region about my lips prominent...

@8249. The first speech in every Earth has been speech by the face, and this from two origins = from the lips, and from the eyes.

@9914. "A lip shall be to its mouth round about" (Exodus 28:32) = what is terminated and closed on every side. "A lip," or border, around the mouth or upper opening of the robe (signifies this), because that "lip," or border, which was round about, did terminate and close it.

Lipothamia.; Lipothamia. @CL 253[2]. @470[2]. @TCR 665[4].

