Little.; Exiguus.

@AC 684. Like a little Heaven. @911[2].

@4255. From little, much. Signified, Explained.

@4279[2]. A Heaven in a little form. @9278[3].

@5704. A Heaven in the least form.

@AR 559. "Knowing that he has a little time" (Revelation 12:12). Explained. ( = because the state has been changed. @AE 755.)

@AE 316[16]. "A little horn" (Daniel 8:9)... It is called "little" because this (doctrine) does not appear to be false. (Compare @AE 316[15].)

@815[7]. Why the Lord called His disciples men "of little faith." Explained.

Little.; Parvus.
Littleness.; Parvitas.

@AC 1396[end]. (They said) he could not agree with them, who were little.

@1763[3]. The little Spirits (of the moon). @9232[end].

@2384. "From little even to great" (Genesis 19:11) = in particular and in general. @8718.

@2429. ("The city) is little" (verse 20) = that it was allowable from the little (of truth) which he had. Explained. @2431.

@8948. (The Spirits of Saturn) esteem themselves as relatively little; and therefore in the other life they appear little.

@9441[2]. A space of invisible littleness.

@HH 420. (The notion that Heaven is little.)

@AR 178. "Thou hast a little power" (Revelation 3:8) = they know that they can avail nothing from themselves.

@527. "Small and great" (Revelation 11:18) = those who in a less and greater degree fear the Lord. (Compare @604. @810. @866.)

@TCR 103[end]. The Spiritual is like itself in a little volume as in a great one.

@533[2]. These two loves (of dominion and possessing) can reign more with the small than the great...

@SE 1249. See <Great>. @AE 696. @836. @1212.

@3242. a. [end]. They supposed themselves great, although so small.

@3586. A certain little one thrust them down.

@3647. Those on high seem to themselves, and also appear to me, small; for the one phantasy produces the other.

@3718. a. Small naked riders seen.

@3804. He emerged a snowy little something.

@4506[end]. The profane were then seen small...

@AE 396. "That they should rest yet for a little time" (Revelation 6:11) = still some duration in that state.

@439[5]. His innocence... is signified by "little Benjamin" (Psalms 68:27). ( = the innocence of the natural man. @449[9].)

@543[13]. In the Spiritual World, when those who are in a persuasion of their own eminence look at others, they see them as little and vile, and the latter also seem such to themselves. Signified.

@624[end]. To "give one of the little ones to drink..." (Matthew 10:42) = to teach innocence from innocence... "Little ones" = the innocent; and, abstractedly, innocence.

Little, A.; Parum.
