@9336. "By little, by little I will drive them out" (Exodus 23:30) = removal by degrees according to order. Explained. @AE 650[59].

@HH 349. Those with whom there has been but little of affection and longing, receive but little.

Little.; Pusillus.

@AC 1008[3]. Occurs. @1066. @1071[4]. @SE 1764. @3168. @3206.

@3551. @AE 1100[8].

@5608[5]. "See that ye despise not one of these little ones." Explained. @HH 277[2]. Content with few and little things.

@AR 315. That the estimation of good and truth is so little as to be scarcely any. Signified.

@DLove 17[end]. If a man by combat against evils as sins has acquired anything spiritual in the world, even although it is little, he is saved; and its uses afterwards grow like "the grain of mustard..."

Little.; Tantillus. @AC 875[4]. @TCR 630.

Little Book.; Libellus.

@AC 10612[end]. To give a bill of divorce.

@AR 469. "He had in his hand a little book open" (Revelation 10:2) = the Word as to this matter of doctrine there, - that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth, and that His Human is Divine. Explained. @479[end]. @480.

@472. The contents of the little book stated.

@481. To "receive the little book" = to receive the doctrine concerning the Lord; to "devour it" = to acknowledge that doctrine; to "make the belly bitter" = that from falsifications it would be ungrateful and annoying; to be "in the mouth sweet as honey" = that the first of reception is grateful and delightful. Explained.

@AE 599. "A little book open" = the Word manifested. Explained. @614. @615. @616. @617. @620.

